# isonicotinic_acid.msf
# Isonicotinic acid (pyridine-4-carboxylic acid, isonicotinic acid)
# pKa1=1.840 (pyridinium NH+, q=+1→0)  pKa2=4.860 (carboxylate, q=0→-1)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# Para isomer of nicotinic acid (which has err=-1.13 and -1.43).
# The 4-COOH is in conjugation with the ring N, shifting both pKa values
# relative to nicotinic acid and pyridine. Two steps with distinct
# ΔBO_ring patterns: step1 is pyridinium N-base, step2 is carboxylate.

